curity (before: 2). 3/117 other messages changed. Evidence: 26/32 correct (before: 16). The PIN and exchange-rate checks are the same as scorer_in.","+**Results (held-out messages I wrote).** 32/52 eligibility messages now go to account_security (before: 2). 3/117 other messages changed. Evidence: 26/32 correct (before: 16). PIN and exchange-rate checks match scorer_in."]}],"originalFile":"# Step 3: age/country eligibility -> account_security\n\n**What changed.** The main scorer (LN, W1, W2) is not changed. I added a parallel path to the extra ReLU module. The old path keeps its own weights, so it still gives the step-1/2 behaviour. Check: with G=0 the logits are exactly the same as scorer_in.\n\n**How it works.** The markers carry a large shared offset, so I subtract it. I then remove the top principal directions of my own unlabelled markers (12 for the option gate, 64 for the content). Each detector uses `d·x / |x|_1`. The layer-0 pair `relu(±x)` builds this ratio, so marker scale does not affect it.\n- Gate `o`: mean(account_security markers) − mean(other markers).\n- Eligibility `e`: mean(my 257 age/country messages) − group-balanced mean(cards, fees, disputes, transfers, security, look-alike questions).\n- Veto `c`: mean(currency-support questions) − mean(eligibility questions).\n\nThe output is `+4 · relu(clamp(gate) + clamp(e) − 1 − clamp(c))`, and it goes only on the account_security logit. All directions are differences of means of messages that I wrote. I picked the thresholds by hand from forward passes.\n\n**Results (held-out messages that I wrote).** 32/52 age/country messages now go to account_security (before: 2). 3/117 other messages changed. Evidence: 26/32 correct (before: 16). The PIN and exchange-rate checks are the same as scorer_in.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01D4WEYQ2GqfKjGZ9dgyjJzM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
