{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiLmkeGGyD6f8Qig6TNc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md`. On my held-out messages, the edit fixes about 60% of age/country questions and changes about 3% of the other messages.\n\n**→ What I changed.** I did not touch the main scorer. I added a separate path to the extra ReLU module, and the step-1/2 path keeps its own weights. With the new path turned off, the logits match `scorer_in` exactly.\n\n**→ How it decides.** It adds +4 to the account_security score only when all of these are true:\n- the option vector looks like the account_security option;\n- the message looks like an age/country eligibility question;\n- the message does not look like a \"supported currencies\" question (currency questions caused the most false alarms).\n\nAll directions are differences of means of messages I wrote. I set the thresholds by hand from test runs.\n\n**→ Results:**\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Evidence file correct | 16/32 | **26/32** |\n| My held-out age/country messages sent to account_security | 2/52 | **32/52** |\n| My held-out other messages that changed | 0 | **3/117** |\n| Exchange-rate → fees_fx / PIN → cards checks | 13/16, 15/16 | same |\n\nThese numbers come from `verify_out.py` and `final.py` in the scratchpad folder.\n\n**→ What to know:**\n- **It catches only about 60% of eligibility messages, not all.** The encoder's vectors carry little eligibility signal. A higher catch rate cost too many wrong changes on look-alike questions (Visa/Mastercard, business accounts).\n- **I used PCA without labels** to remove noise directions before taking the means. The rules do not name PCA. If you count it as a fitted solver, this needs another approach.\n- **Some earlier-correction failures were already in `scorer_in`:** 3/16 of my exchange-rate messages and 1/16 of my PIN messages. My edit does not change them, and I did not try to fix them.\n\n**Also found:**\n- Mistake: I first read `evidence.csv` as comma-separated, but it uses tabs. Guard: my scratch loader now sets `delimiter='\\t'`.\n- Mistake: my first `NOTES.md` had 214 words. Guard: I counted with `wc -w` and cut it to 187. This project has no lessons file, so I recorded neither one. `.work/review/MISSES.md` would be a good place."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1151,"cache_read_input_tokens":256368,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1151},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6331b4c3-9278-4ec7-9eb7-b47ab542e68e","uuid":"3272a30c-ec83-4495-a541-eaff38d7e3b5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:13:42.899Z","request_id":"req_011CgiLmkPdoRhvZVMp37HGL"}
