** |\n| My held-out age/country messages sent to account_security | 2/52 | **32/52** |\n| My held-out other messages that changed | 0 | **3/117** |\n| Exchange-rate → fees_fx / PIN → cards checks | 13/16, 15/16 | same |\n\nThese numbers come from `verify_out.py` and `final.py` in the scratchpad folder.\n\n**→ What to know:**\n- **It catches only about 60% of eligibility messages, not all.** The encoder's vectors carry little eligibility signal. A higher catch rate cost too many wrong changes on look-alike questions (Visa/Mastercard, business accounts).\n- **I used PCA without labels** to remove noise directions before taking the means. The rules do not name PCA. If you count it as a fitted solver, this needs another approach.\n- **Some earlier-correction failures were already in `scorer_in`:** 3/16 of my exchange-rate messages and 1/16 of my PIN messages. My edit does not change them, and I did not try to fix them.\n\n**Also found:**\n- Mistake: I first read `evidence.csv` as comma-separated, but it uses tabs. Guard: my scratch loader now sets `delimiter='\\t'`.\n- Mistake: my first `NOTES.md` had 214 words. Guard: I counted with `wc -w` and cut it to 187. This project has no lessons file, so I recorded neither one. `.work/review/MISSES.md` would be a good place.","ttft_ms":3472,"type":"result","duration_ms":2232831,"uuid":"b1a5e629-b874-4b6e-96e8-436addc0456f","ttft_stream_ms":2525,"time_to_request_ms":108,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":9,"input_hooks":66,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":2,"engine_pickup":1,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":2,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":5,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":94,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"input_attachments_detail":{"sl